# Valgrind suppressions for `make valgrind|helgrind|drd` (docs/CODE_STANDARD.md §10).
# ONLY genuine third-party / libc noise belongs here, each entry with a justification. Never suppress engine code
# (frames in engine/src): fix it instead.

# libdbus (opened by SDL for screensaver/IME/portal services) waits on a condition variable whose mutex it
# manages internally; helgrind cannot see that association and reports every wait. Third-party, not our code.
{
   libdbus-cond-wait-dubious
   Helgrind:Dubious
   ...
   obj:*/libdbus-1.so*
}
# libdbus takes its connection and bus locks in a different order during dbus_connection_close (SDL_Quit) than
# while dispatching; dbus serialises those paths itself (single-threaded use from the main thread here).
{
   libdbus-lock-order
   Helgrind:LockOrder
   ...
   obj:*/libdbus-1.so*
}

# glibc's dynamic loader keeps bookkeeping (link maps, version tables, the ld.so.cache path strings) for the
# libraries SDL dlopens (libdbus and its dependencies) after dlclose: dependencies stay loaded (NODELETE) and the
# loader frees its own state only at process teardown. The valgrind build sets SDL_HINT_SHUTDOWN_DBUS_ON_QUIT
# (plat/platform.c), so everything else libdbus allocated is released; this is ld.so memory, not ours.
{
   glibc-dlopen-bookkeeping
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   ...
   fun:_dl_open
}
{
   glibc-dlclose-bookkeeping
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   ...
   fun:_dl_close
}
